-- Q854: Privacy Requirements and Data Protection [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Data minimization, codified in GDPR Article 5 Section 1(c), requires that personal data be adequate, relevant, and limited to what is necessary for the specified processing purpose. Collecting SSNs, marital status, and political affiliation when only name and date of birth are needed far exceeds what is necessary.
Wrong (B): Purpose limitation under GDPR Article 5 Section 1(b) restricts how previously collected data may be used for new purposes, not the volume collected at the point of collection.
Wrong (C): Storage limitation governs how long data is retained, not how much is collected initially.
Wrong (D): Integrity and confidentiality addresses data security and accuracy, not the scope of data collection.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 854;

-- Q856: Privacy Requirements and Data Protection [hard/L1]
